@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the eight failing e2e tests, their root causes, and what each one is waiting on
' covers: tests/e2e/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh
'
' Measured: `go test -tags=e2e ./tests/e2e/` on this host — 35 pass, 6 skip, 8 fail,
' 585s. Every failure reproduces on a pristine checkout, so none of them is a
' regression from the decomposition; they are the baseline that has to be repaired
' before move 6 (_spec/_plans/main-decomposition-moves.puml) can be judged.
'
' ── C1 · THE ENTRYPOINT DIES BEFORE THE AGENT STARTS (root cause proven) ────
' packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, _proveo_lock_installs:
'
'     exec 9>"${dir}/install.lock" 2>/dev/null || return 0
'
' A redirection failure on `exec` is FATAL to a non-interactive shell, so the
' `|| return 0` is dead code: instead of skipping installs, the whole entrypoint
' exits. Measured on proveo/claudecode with the working-tree entrypoint:
'   * installs enabled  → exit 1 after 1s, `set -x` ends on `+ exec`, and
'     PROVEO_SMOKE_READY never prints
'   * PROVEO_AUTO_INSTALL_TOOLS=false → the same entrypoint reaches
'     PROVEO_SMOKE_READY and holds, exactly as the probe expects
' The helper works when called on its own, so the trigger is state the run leaves
' behind before it — most likely the lock file's owner after the runtime-user step.
' FIX: probe writability first and never let `exec` decide the run's fate:
'     if ! : >>"${dir}/install.lock" 2>/dev/null; then return 0; fi
'     exec 9>>"${dir}/install.lock"
' plus a container test that asserts an unwritable lock path SKIPS installs rather
' than ending the run. `ensure_project_tools` is shared by every harness, so run
' the same probe per def rather than assuming claudecode is the only victim.
' UNBLOCKS: TestClaudecodeEntrypointOperatesOnTheInputDir, and very likely the
' claudecode leg of TestHelloWorldE2E and TestPromptfulE2E — an agent whose
' entrypoint exited cannot answer a prompt or write a file.
'
' ── C2 · FOUR ASSERTIONS PIN THE RETIRED HOME REDIRECT ──────────────────────
' sbxHome DELETES HOME and PROVEO_HOME on the sandbox backend and publishes
' PROVEO_STATE_HOME instead. That deletion IS the fix: redirecting HOME orphaned
' the credential sbx's own proxy writes under the image's home, and the agent then
' reported "Not logged in". Three tests still assert the redirect:
'   TestProveoHomePersistence ("agent cmd missing -e HOME=")
'   TestSandboxKitIsAMixinCarryingNoCredentials ("Kit environment omits HOME")
'   TestSandboxBackendCarriesProveoHomeBesideHome (the name is the old contract)
' FIX: assert the CURRENT contract — no HOME/PROVEO_HOME in the sbx argv or Kit,
' PROVEO_STATE_HOME present and pointing at the mounted home, and the docker path
' unchanged. Keep one assertion that the redirect stays gone, so it cannot return
' by accident. This is a rewrite of what is asserted, not a loosening: each one
' gains a positive claim it did not have.
'
' ── C3 · TWO FAILURES ENCODE OPEN DECISIONS — DO NOT MAKE THEM GREEN ────────
' These two are the live evidence behind _spec/_plans/revision-env-egress.puml.
' Flipping either to match today's behaviour would erase the finding.
'
'   TestEveryHarnessGetsTheDockerAccessItPromises  (decision D2)
'     asserts no socket and no daemon inside an sbx sandbox; the probe reports
'     HAS-SOCKET and SERVER:29.7.2 for claudecode and cursor, because the images
'     now carry com.docker.sandboxes.start-docker. Code and test assert opposite
'     things about one decision. It goes green when D2 is decided: either the
'     label is gated like dind, or this assertion is rewritten to "a daemon is
'     present AND its containers cannot leave the Kit allowlist".
'
'   TestCredentialForwardingIntegrity  (decision D1)
'     asserts no provider key appears in the sandbox argv; proveo deliberately
'     emits `-e VAR=` (empty) to override sbx's GLOBAL secret store. The empty
'     value is also how a workspace .env refills a variable proveo blanked. It
'     goes green when D1 lands: assert `-e VAR=` carries no VALUE, and add the
'     sentinel parity the plan proposes.
'
' ── C4 · WHAT IS LEFT AFTER C1 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' TestHelloWorldE2E (opencode, cecli legs) and TestPromptfulE2E run the local
' model. Re-measure them once C1 lands; on macOS the local-model posture drops to
' a CPU-only sidecar outside open+forward, which is slow enough to look like a
' hang. Only then decide whether they need a posture fix or a longer deadline.
'
' ── ACCEPTANCE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Green does NOT mean zero red. It means: C1 and C2 pass, C4 passes or states a
' measured environmental reason, and the only red left is C3 — where each failure
' names the decision it is waiting on. A suite in that state is a baseline a
' refactor can be judged against, because every red has an owner.
title PLANNED — restoring a readable e2e baseline: 8 failures, 4 causes, 1 that must stay red

component "go test -tags=e2e ./tests/e2e/\n35 pass · 6 skip · 8 fail · 585s" as SUITE <<error>>

frame "C1 · one shell line ends every run" as C1 <<host>> {
  component "_proveo_lock_installs\n`exec 9>lock || return 0` — the guard is\ndead code; the redirect kills the shell" as LOCK <<error>>
  component "probe writability, then exec\n+ a test for the unwritable case" as FIXLOCK <<app>>
}

frame "C2 · assertions pin a retired contract" as C2 <<host>> {
  component "3 tests assert -e HOME=\nsbxHome deletes it on purpose" as HOMEA <<error>>
  component "assert PROVEO_STATE_HOME instead,\nand that the redirect stays gone" as FIXHOME <<app>>
}

frame "C3 · decision-bearing, keep red" as C3 <<host>> {
  component "docker access promise (D2)\nHAS-SOCKET · SERVER:29.7.2" as D2 <<error>>
  component "credential argv (D1)\n`-e VAR=` is deliberate" as D1 <<error>>
}

frame "C4 · measure again after C1" as C4 <<host>> {
  component "HelloWorld · Promptful\nlocal model, CPU sidecar on macOS" as MODEL <<async>>
}

SUITE ARROW_ERROR LOCK
SUITE ARROW_ERROR HOMEA
SUITE ARROW_ERROR D2
SUITE ARROW_ERROR D1
LOCK ARROW_MAIN FIXLOCK
HOMEA ARROW_MAIN FIXHOME
FIXLOCK ARROW_QUEUE MODEL : re-measure
D2 ARROW_OPTIONAL SUITE : green when D2 lands
D1 ARROW_OPTIONAL SUITE : green when D1 lands

note bottom of LOCK
  Proven by measurement, not by reading: installs
  on gives exit 1 in one second with the trace
  ending on `+ exec`; installs off reaches
  PROVEO_SMOKE_READY and holds.
end note

note bottom of FIXHOME
  A rewrite, not a loosening. Each of the three
  gains a positive claim it lacked — that
  PROVEO_STATE_HOME points at the mounted home and
  that the old redirect cannot come back.
end note

note bottom of C3
  Both reds are findings. Matching them to today's
  behaviour deletes the only evidence that the
  sandbox ships a daemon, and that a blanked
  credential can be refilled from the workspace.
end note

note bottom of SUITE
  The bar is not zero red. It is: every red names
  the decision it waits on. That is a baseline a
  refactor can be judged against, because a new
  failure is then unmistakable.
end note
@enduml
